{*
	{templateType} names a class whose properties are the template's variables,
	which is how a Nette project types a whole template at once. Nothing in this
	file may be underlined, and Ctrl-click on the class name has to open
	app/Presenters/ArticleTemplate.php.

	The point of the file is the step after that: $heading and $articles are
	declared nowhere in the template, so they are defined only if the plugin
	reads them out of the class.
*}
{templateType App\Presenters\ArticleTemplate}

<h1>{$heading}</h1>

<ul>
	<li n:foreach="$articles as $article">{$article->getTitle()}</li>
</ul>

<p n:if="$articles">{$articles|length} articles</p>
